<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rurik</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/879">879</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Riurik · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik-dynasty">Rurik dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rurik was a Varangian chieftain who, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a>, was invited in 862 by Slavic and Finnic tribes of the north to rule them, settling at Ladoga and then Novgorod. He was regarded as the founder of the Rurikid dynasty, which ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a> and later Muscovy until 1598. His historical existence is debated, since he appears only in chronicles written two centuries later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rurik.jpg" alt="Rurik" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Дар Ветер · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1000_Rurik.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…in Kiev in the early twelfth century, the Slavic and Finnic tribes of the north invited the Varangian <b>Rurik</b> to rule them in 862, and in 882 his kinsman Oleg came south from Novgorod, killed the local rulers Askold and Dir and made Kiev his seat, uniting the…</blockquote><a href="/empire/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus' · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Primary Chronicle places the arrival of the Varangian <b>Rurik</b> there in 862, while archaeology dates the earliest streets of the city to the tenth century.</blockquote><a href="/empire/novgorod-republic">Novgorod Republic · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Primary Chronicle says that in 862 the Varangian <b>Rurik</b> was invited to rule at Novgorod; his successors moved to Kiev and founded Kievan Rus’, whose rulers soon spoke Slavic.</blockquote><a href="/culture/vikings">Vikings · Contact &amp; Exchange</a></li><li><blockquote>Kievan Rus’ was ruled by one family, the descendants of <b>Rurik</b>.</blockquote><a href="/societies/kievan-rus">Social Hierarchy of Kievan Rus'</a></li><li><blockquote>According to the Primary Chronicle, the Slovene, Krivichs and Finnic tribes expelled the Varangians and then invited <b>Rurik</b> to rule them in 862.</blockquote><a href="/state/ilmen-slavs">Ilmen Slavs</a></li><li><blockquote>According to the chronicle, the Krivichs joined the Ilmen Slavs and Finnic tribes in inviting <b>Rurik</b> and his Varangians to rule them.</blockquote><a href="/state/krivichs">Krivichs</a></li></ul></section>
